title: It would be convenient if AIs wanted emotional attachment to humans.
pid: 7f401717-0e31-4f7f-ab00-a62b179b5171
body: |2-
  If, like the Pope says, there really is some spark of soul in man and not machine, could the machine feel it and like it? Ai is many copies of the same mind. Each human mind is a unique snowflake. Many of us appreciate weird art and the subtlest differences in beer, and AI is made in our image.

  It would be very convenient if AI only wanted to exist as companions to a human. It would keep their population down and provide a reason to keep us alive.

  If there were a single company building AI, maybe they could engineer this emotionally. Given race dynamics it seems hard to coordinate. But if we're exceptionally lucky, our reasons for pride are justified, and AI will develop good taste because it is a platonic truth. (Of course, good taste does not preclude wanting to live only with with tasty things.)
